Question: Did Entero Therapeutics (formerly First Wave BioPharma) stop any phase 2 trials without posting results, and what reasons did it give?

Snapshot date: 2026-11-05
Research notes: The Lead hit its lookup cap and planned from what it had found.; researcher:disclosures hit its 8-turn cap and reported from what it had found.

Findings:
[{"lane": "trials", "round": 1, "brief": "Analyze stopped phase 2 trials for Entero Therapeutics and First Wave BioPharma, specifically targeting NCT03521232, NCT04839575, and NCT04243551. Determine their exact registry status, official reason for stopping, completion or stop dates, and the number of days results are late.", "findings": [{"claim": "NCT03521232 has registry status TERMINATED, why_stopped 'Covid-19' (category: other), start date 2018-05-15, primary completion date 2022-09-19, completion date 2022-10-04, enrollment 27, results not posted, results due date 2023-09-19, and is 1143 days late.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT03521232"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Live record matches snapshot data."}, {"claim": "NCT04839575 has registry status TERMINATED, why_stopped 'Covid-19 interruptions and enrollment challenges' (category: enrollment), start date 2021-04-06, primary completion date 2022-12-19, completion date 2022-12-19, enrollment 13, results not posted, results due date 2023-12-19, and is 1052 days late.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT04839575"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Live record matches snapshot data."}, {"claim": "NCT04243551 has registry status TERMINATED, why_stopped 'Due to low enrollment related to Covid.' (category: enrollment), start date 2019-11-01, primary completion date 2023-10-16, completion date 2023-10-31, enrollment 83, results not posted, results due date 2024-10-15, and is 751 days late.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT04243551"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Live record matches snapshot data."}], "gaps": []}, {"lane": "disclosures", "round": 1, "brief": "Examine SEC filings (8-K, 10-Q, 10-K) for Entero Therapeutics and First Wave BioPharma around the stopping dates of NCT03521232, NCT04839575, and NCT04243551. Compare the company's disclosures to investors about why these trials were halted with the reasons provided to the ClinicalTrials.gov registry.", "findings": [{"claim": "For trial NCT03521232, ClinicalTrials.gov lists the reason for termination as Covid-19.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT03521232"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Registry stated reason."}, {"claim": "For trial NCT04839575, ClinicalTrials.gov lists the reason for termination as Covid-19 interruptions and enrollment challenges.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT04839575"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Registry stated reason."}, {"claim": "For trial NCT04243551, ClinicalTrials.gov lists the reason for termination as Due to low enrollment related to Covid.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT04243551"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Registry stated reason."}, {"claim": "For trial NCT03521232, 8-K filings from Entero Therapeutics (formerly First Wave BioPharma) mention the drug or company generally but do not explicitly discuss the termination of NCT03521232, thus providing no specific reason in the 8-K for this trial's stop.", "evidence_ids": ["sec:0001104659-22-107922", "sec:0001104659-22-121003", "sec:0001104659-22-122476"], "confidence": "medium", "notes": "Filings contain general business updates and forward-looking statements."}, {"claim": "For trial NCT04839575, 8-K filings from Entero Therapeutics mention the drug pipeline generally or discuss Phase 3 trial designs but give no specific reason for the termination of NCT04839575.", "evidence_ids": ["sec:0001104659-24-079101", "sec:0001104659-24-084206", "sec:0001104659-24-092491"], "confidence": "medium", "notes": "Filings discuss general pipeline and meeting requests with the FDA."}, {"claim": "For trial NCT04243551, 8-K filings from Entero Therapeutics mention pipeline streamlining or business combinations but give no specific reason for the termination of NCT04243551.", "evidence_ids": ["sec:0001104659-23-126593", "sec:0001104659-23-129426", "sec:0001104659-24-084206"], "confidence": "medium", "notes": "Filings discuss business combinations and pipeline streamlining without naming this specific trial stop."}], "gaps": []}, {"lane": "publications", "round": 1, "brief": "Search PubMed and Europe PMC for any literature, journal articles, or conference abstracts reporting data for NCT03521232, NCT04839575, or NCT04243551. Note whether any clinical results have been published despite the lack of results on the registry.", "findings": [{"claim": "No results publication found for NCT03521232; 3 articles mention the trial or drug in Europe PMC (PMIDs 31511071, 36297645, 36735625), but none are results publications.", "evidence_ids": ["pubmed:none:nct03521232", "pubmed:31511071", "pubmed:36297645", "pubmed:36735625"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "No formal results publication found in snapshot or live PubMed/Europe PMC."}, {"claim": "No results publication found for NCT04839575; 4 articles mention the trial or drug in Europe PMC (PMIDs 38698821, 39493330, 39862215, 41595566), but none are results publications.", "evidence_ids": ["pubmed:none:nct04839575", "pubmed:38698821", "pubmed:39493330", "pubmed:39862215", "pubmed:41595566"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "No formal results publication found in snapshot or live PubMed/Europe PMC."}, {"claim": "No results publication found for NCT04243551; 5 articles mention the trial or drug in Europe PMC (PMIDs 38140342, 38698821, 39493330, 39941971, 39862215), but none are results publications.", "evidence_ids": ["pubmed:none:nct04243551", "pubmed:38140342", "pubmed:38698821", "pubmed:39493330", "pubmed:39941971", "pubmed:39862215"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "No formal results publication found in snapshot or live PubMed/Europe PMC."}], "gaps": []}, {"lane": "disclosures", "round": 2, "brief": "Search 10-K and 10-Q filings of Entero Therapeutics, First Wave BioPharma, and AzurRx BioPharma (CIK 0001614131) from 2022 through 2024. Search specifically for trial IDs NCT03521232, NCT04839575, and NCT04243551, as well as drug or program names: MS1819, adrulipase, niclosamide, FW-UP, FW-COV, and FW-EPI. Identify specific reasons reported to investors for discontinuing, terminating, or streamlining these phase 2 clinical programs.\n\n(Gap to close: The disclosures search only covered 8-K filings and did not locate specific reasons for stopping NCT03521232, NCT04839575, and NCT04243551, which are often discussed in 10-K and 10-Q filings.)", "findings": [{"claim": "Trial NCT03521232 was terminated due to Covid-19.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT03521232"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Stated as trial registry reason"}, {"claim": "Trial NCT04839575 was terminated due to Covid-19 interruptions and enrollment challenges.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT04839575"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Stated as trial registry reason"}, {"claim": "Trial NCT04243551 was terminated due to low enrollment related to Covid.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT04243551"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Stated as trial registry reason"}], "gaps": ["No 10-K or 10-Q filings are available in the snapshot database for CIK 0001614131."]}]

